X86_64 SpinlockCmpxchg3
(* Compare-and-swap spinlock on x86-TSO (see spinlock_cmpxchg2.kl):
   `lock cmpxchg` acquire loop, plain-store release. Three threads each
   increment a shared counter once under the lock.
   Property: counter = 3 in every final state.
   Proved for every layout of the runner's image, the code verbatim
   (`decls = {}`): `CmpxAbs.x64_cmpx_counter_envG_verbatim`
   (Promising/SLR/EnvG/X64CmpxAbsPublic.lean). Proved from the runner's
   exact configuration (declarations and initial memory included):
   `CmpxAbs.x64_cmpx_counter_envG_runner` (X64CmpxAbsRunner.lean), with a
   `.Concrete` instance.
   Proved no fault at the runner's declarations (rule-level):
   `CmpxAbs.x64_cmpx_counter_envG_runner_noFault`
   (Promising/SLR/EnvG/X64NoFaultDLocks.lean), with a `.Concrete` instance.
   The shared symbols are typed (`uint32_t`) so that the runner declares
   them as sized locations at the width of the code's accesses (DECLS): the
   runner's declarations then agree with the proofs'
   locations. The code block and the verdict are unchanged.
   Proved (fault freedom at the runner's declarations, MEMVALS):
   `CmpxAbs.x64_cmpx_counter_envG_runner_faultFree`
   (Promising/SLR/EnvG/X64FaultFreeFixed.lean), with a `.Concrete` instance.
   Proved (LIVESPINX): promise-free deadlock-freedom on a valid layout
   of the image (`[ValidLayout (layout cmpxImageV)]`):
   `Live.SpinX64CmpxPF.spin_cmpx_live_pf : CmpxSpinLivePF fuel`, at the
   runner's layout `spin_cmpx_live_pf_concrete` and from its start state
   `spin_cmpx_live_pf_runnerN`; one-shot form `spin_cmpx_live_oneShot_pf`
   (Promising/LiveSpinX64CmpxPF.lean).
   Proved (LIVESPINXSEM): deadlock-freedom with promises on the machine
   with semantic certification, every fuel, under `WeakFairSem ∧ MemFair`
   (`MemFair` a modelling assumption on x86), on a valid layout:
   `Live.SpinX64SemCmpx.spin_cmpx_live_sem : CmpxSpinLiveSem fuel`, at the
   runner's layout `spin_cmpx_live_sem_concrete`; one-shot form
   `spin_cmpx_live_oneShot_sem` (Promising/LiveSpinX64SemCmpx.lean). The
   `CmpxSpinLive` (over `succs`, incomplete `certify`) stays open
   (KNOWN_GAPS.md, "Liveness: spinlocks, x64 (LIVESPINX)").
# flags: -sym -fuel 300
# expect: Always
*)
{
uint32_t lock=0; uint32_t counter=0;
}
threads { P0: worker done; P1: worker done; P2: worker done; }
code {
worker:
  xorl %eax,%eax
  movl $1,%ecx
  lock cmpxchgl %ecx,(lock)
  jne worker
  movl (counter),%edx
  addl $1,%edx
  movl %edx,(counter)
  movl $0,(lock)
  jmp done
done:
}
forall [counter]=3
